snac (Social Networks Are Crap) is a simple, minimalistic ActivityPub
instance written in portable C.  It runs as a daemon, normally behind a
TLS-enabled HTTP server, and implements enough of the ActivityPub and
Mastodon APIs to federate with other Fediverse software.

It is lightweight with minimal dependencies (libcurl and OpenSSL only),
needs no database (all data is stored as plain files) and offers a simple
but effective web interface.  It is multiuser, supports the Mastodon API
so compatible apps can be used, and uses neither JavaScript nor cookies.
